_refine.details
;THE NONSTANDARD UNIT CELL I 2 WAS CHOSEN OVER THE
EQUIVALENT C 2 CELL BECAUSE OF THE CONVENIENCE OF HAVING A
BETA ANGLE NEAR 90 DEGREES AND TO MAINTAIN CONSISTENCY WITH
THE INITIAL CRYSTALLIZATION REPORT.  TO CONVERT FROM
FRACTIONAL I 2 TO FRACTIONAL C 2, USE THE FOLLOWING
TRANSFORMATION:

    [  1.0 ][ 0.0 ][ 0.0 ]   (XFRAC_I2)   (XFRAC_C2)
    [  0.0 ][ 1.0 ][ 0.0 ] X (YFRAC_I2) = (YFRAC_C2)
    [ -1.0 ][ 0.0 ][ 1.0 ]   (ZFRAC_I2)   (ZFRAC_C2)

THE ORTHOGONAL COORDINATE SYSTEM CHOSEN FOR THIS ENTRY
IS THAT DEFINED BY THE LOCAL SYMMETRY OF THE COMPLEX (23).
;
